@northstar-js/maps
Code: MIT (see LICENSE).

The map geometry and names are derived from third-party data, which keeps its own licence:

- Natural Earth 1:50m Cultural Vectors, admin-0 countries — public domain.
  https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/
  Boundaries are Natural Earth de facto lines, drawn for orientation. They are not a political statement.

- world-atlas 2.0.2 (TopoJSON of Natural Earth, data/countries-50m.json) — ISC License,
  Copyright 2013-2019 Michael Bostock. Full text: data/world-atlas-LICENSE.

- i18n-iso-countries 7.14.0 (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2/alpha-3/numeric table, data/codes.json) — MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2016 widdix GmbH. Full text: data/i18n-LICENSE.

- Unicode CLDR 47.0 English country names, read through Node.js Intl.DisplayNames (ICU 77.1) at build time —
  Unicode License v3. https://www.unicode.org/license.txt

Modifications: the TopoJSON is decoded, unwrapped across the antimeridian, simplified and projected
(Equal Earth for the world, Lambert azimuthal equal-area per country). dist/maps/PROVENANCE.md lists every
renamed, slug-keyed, inset and omitted feature.
